# Firecrawl Credit Safety

When writing code that calls Firecrawl tools:

- Always pass `parsers: []` on `firecrawl_scrape_and_extract_from_url` unless PDF parsing is explicitly needed.
- When PDF parsing IS needed, set `maxPages` (e.g., 20) to cap credit usage: `parsers: [{ type: "pdf", mode: "fast", maxPages: 20 }]`.
- In search calls, pass `scrapeOptions: { parsers: [] }` to prevent PDF parsing on search results.
- In crawl calls, pass `scrapeOptions: { parsers: [] }` and set a reasonable `limit` (not the default 10000).
- Use `firecrawl_get_credit_usage` to monitor consumption in long-running agents.
- Use `firecrawl_support_ask` for error diagnosis instead of blind retries.

Credit costs:
- Scrape: 1 credit per page
- Search: 1 credit per 10 results (+ scrape credits if scrapeOptions includes formats)
- Crawl: 1 credit per page crawled
- Batch scrape: 1 credit per URL
- PDF parsing: 1 credit PER PDF PAGE (`parsers: ["pdf"]`) vs 1 FLAT credit (`parsers: []`)
- Map: 1 credit

